  "answer": "The goal was not met: only two of the five challenging cases were confirmed. Both have the lead car 0.5 s late at 0.75x speed: S10 on 09a95ffa and S1 on 023b7fcc. Neither is a rear-end. In every failure the ego slowed behind the lead car, then drifted out of its lane, usually to the left and against a RIGHT command, and hit a car in the next lane. The one exception is a run in S10 where a car from behind hit the ego, and the triage could not tell whether the policy was at fault. So at 2 Hz the retimed lead car causes trouble by making the ego slow down and wander out of its lane, not by being run into. The strongest third candidate, 12855a41 at +1 s and 0.75x (S20), failed in most runs, but its range still reaches below one half. The other five scenes produced no confirmed case: four showed no failures, mostly from single runs, and 19f339ba failed only once at S23.",
